idence":["AC item '[non-codebase] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE. `curl -D -' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the two Summary line citations to where the /mcp/ URL actually appears (docs/mcp-client-setup.md:74/86/95/114/128/137 and examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:22).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4229,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search_files docs/mcp-client-setup.md '/mcp/' returns hits at lines 74,75,86,95,114,128,137,159 — none at 54; line 54 read shows secret-handling prose","examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:22 = 'url = \"https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/\"'; line 18 is a blank comment ('#')"],"finding":"Two supporting line citations in the Summary point at lines that do not contain the documented /mcp/ URL they claim to: docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54 is prose about secret handling (the URL appears at lines 74/86/95/114/128/137), and examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18 is a blank comment line (the url = \"...\\/mcp/\" is at line 22).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda725b358a2827e2","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Summary — 'the docs point AT the affected form (docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54, examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18)'","norm_id":"n44f0c520e0d43d14","priority":0.3771,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader following the citation to confirm the affected form lands on unrelated text"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace 'docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54' with a line that carries the URL (e.g. :74) and 'examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18' with ':22'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the existing parity test (test_autodeploy_mcp_run_new_passes_the_bedrock_region) NOW to assert mcp_run_new carries `-e FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'`, rather than deferring it, since autodeploy.sh is already in scope and the mutation-check should cover this path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Verified by reading that function in the committed script'","'extending it to this var has no test yet and is tracked as follow-up'","The mutation check lists 'FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS in compose' but not the autodeploy docker run flag, so its RED->GREEN is asserted only for compose"],"finding":"The autodeploy FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS parity (criterion 5) is verified only by manual reading of the script, and extending the automated parity test is deferred to follow-up — so a mutation dropping the flag from mcp_run_new would not be caught by any test, despite autodeploy.sh already being in file-impact scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f17ec7293972278b4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, criterion 5 / Testing","norm_id":"nc3fbce12b83f7af8","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit to autodeploy.sh removes -e FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*' from mcp_run_new; compose still has it so the compose parity test stays green, but deployed containers silently re-open the HTTPS->HTTP downgrade on the blue-green path."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add an assertion to the already-in-scope parity test that mcp_run_new's argv contains `-e FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'`, and include dropping that flag in the mutation-check list so RED->GREEN covers the deploy path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the existing autodeploy parity test now (rather than deferring) to assert `mcp_run_new` carries `-e FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'`, so the ship-critical deploy path is regression-protected by an automated assertion, not manual reading.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"extending it to this var has no test yet and is tracked as follow-up\"","\"autodeploy.sh starts the MCP container with a bare docker run (mcp_run_new), not compose, so a compose-only env var never reaches a deployed container, leaving the fix inert on the path MCP ships through\""],"finding":"The blue-green deploy path change (adding `-e FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'` to `autodeploy.sh`'s `mcp_run_new`) is the path MCP actually ships through, yet its verification is only 'by reading that function in the committed script' — the automated parity assertion is explicitly deferred as follow-up ('has no test yet and is tracked as follow-up'). A future edit to mcp_run_new that drops the flag would re-open the downgrade on deployed containers with no test catching it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85bac8264d359645","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, criterion 5; Testing section","norm_id":"nde6ced0dd1880556","priority":0.0,"reaso